<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="generator" content="dummyrun {{.ToolVersion}}">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{asset "mark.svg"}}">
<!--
Typefaces: Space Grotesk, Copyright 2020 The Space Grotesk Project Authors (https://github.com/floriankarsten/space-grotesk),
and Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, Copyright 2020 Braille Institute of America, Inc. Both are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(https://openfontlicense.org). They are subset and embedded below.
-->
<style>
@font-face { font-family: "Space Grotesk"; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500 700; font-display: swap; src: url("{{asset "space-grotesk.woff2"}}") format("woff2"); }
@font-face { font-family: "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next"; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400 700; font-display: swap; src: url("{{asset "atkinson-hyperlegible-next.woff2"}}") format("woff2"); }

:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --paper: #ffffff;
  --ink: #1d1d1b;
  --muted: #55524d;
  --rule: #d9d6cf;
  --panel: #f5f3ee;
  --amber: #fbad18;
  --link: #7d5200;
  --focus: #1d1d1b;
  --blocker: #b3192f; --blocker-bg: #fdeaec; --blocker-ink: #7a0a1e;
  --major: #b85c00;   --major-bg: #ffecd2;   --major-ink: #6b3400;
  --minor: #946f00;   --minor-bg: #fff5c4;   --minor-ink: #5a4500;
  --info: #4f7a9b;    --info-bg: #e5eff7;    --info-ink: #1c3d5a;
  --good-bg: #e3f1e6; --good-ink: #0d3d1b;
  --font-heading: "Space Grotesk", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-body: "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
}
@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --paper: #161616;
    --ink: #f3f1ec;
    --muted: #b5b1a8;
    --rule: #3a3936;
    --panel: #1f1f1e;
    --link: #fbad18;
    --focus: #f3f1ec;
    --blocker: #ff7b72; --blocker-bg: #3a1a1d; --blocker-ink: #ffb9b3;
    --major: #ffa657;   --major-bg: #3a2612;   --major-ink: #ffd3a6;
    --minor: #e3b341;   --minor-bg: #33290b;   --minor-ink: #f0da8e;
    --info: #8fb6d4;    --info-bg: #1c2a36;    --info-ink: #c3dcee;
    --good-bg: #16301d; --good-ink: #a8e3b8;
  }
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { font-size: 100%; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-size-adjust: 100%; background: var(--paper); }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-rendering: optimizeLegibility; }
a { color: var(--link); text-underline-offset: 0.18em; text-decoration-thickness: 0.08em; }
a:focus-visible, .skip:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 2px; }
.skip { position: absolute; left: 0.75rem; top: -5rem; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); padding: 0.6rem 1rem; z-index: 10; border-radius: 6px; }
.skip:focus { top: 0.75rem; }
.wrap { max-width: 54rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; }
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5 { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
h2 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }
h4 { font-size: 1.15rem; }
h5 { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem; }
p, ul, ol, dl, table, figure { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
p, li { max-width: 68ch; }
code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.05em 0.35em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.muted { color: var(--muted); }
section { padding: 3rem 0 0.5rem; }
section > h2::before { content: ""; display: block; width: 2.5rem; height: 0.3rem; background: var(--amber); border-radius: 2px; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

/* Cover */
.cover { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem; }
.cover .wrap { position: relative; }
.cover-top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
.cover-brand { display: block; width: 11rem; height: auto; }
.cover-brand img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
.cover-brand .logo-dark { display: none; }
@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .cover-brand .logo-light { display: none; } .cover-brand .logo-dark { display: block; } }
.eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
.cover h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 1.7rem + 3.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.025em; max-width: 18ch; margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
.cover .for { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.cover-body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem; align-items: end; }
.cover-body.has-mascot { grid-template-columns: 1fr 9.5rem; }
.mascot { width: 9.5rem; height: auto; }
.cover-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr)); gap: 1rem 2rem; border-top: 3px solid var(--amber); padding-top: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
.cover-meta div { min-width: 0; }
dt.k, .cover-meta dt { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
.cover-meta dd { margin: 0.15rem 0 0; font-size: 1.0625rem; }
.cover-lead { font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
.overview { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.2rem; max-width: 40rem; }
.overview h2, .overview .ov-title { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; }
.overview h2::before { display: none; }
.bar { display: block; width: 100%; height: 0.85rem; border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden; margin: 0 0 0.85rem; background: var(--rule); }
.seg { stroke: var(--panel); stroke-width: 2px; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
.seg-blocker { fill: var(--blocker); } .seg-major { fill: var(--major); } .seg-minor { fill: var(--minor); } .seg-info { fill: var(--info); }
.chips { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 0.5rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.chips li { max-width: none; }
.chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; border: 1.5px solid; border-radius: 99px; padding: 0.1rem 0.8rem 0.1rem 0.55rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 700; }
.chip b { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.05rem; }
.chip.is-zero { border-style: dashed; font-weight: 400; }

/* Severity colours. Every use also carries the severity as words. */
.b-blocker { background: var(--blocker-bg); color: var(--blocker-ink); border-color: var(--blocker); }
.b-major { background: var(--major-bg); color: var(--major-ink); border-color: var(--major); }
.b-minor { background: var(--minor-bg); color: var(--minor-ink); border-color: var(--minor); }
.b-info { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info-ink); border-color: var(--info); }
.badge { display: inline-block; border: 1.5px solid; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0 0.55rem; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0.35rem 0.25rem 0; vertical-align: middle; }
.st-confirmed { background: var(--good-bg); color: var(--good-ink); border-color: var(--good-ink); }
.st-not-reviewed { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); border: 1.5px dashed var(--muted); }
.bl-new { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info-ink); border-color: var(--info); }
.bl-still-present, .bl-fixed { background: var(--panel); color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--muted); }

/* Contents */
.contents { padding: 2rem 0 0; }
.contents h2 { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
.contents h2::before { display: none; }
.contents > ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: toc; }
.contents > ol > li { counter-increment: toc; max-width: none; padding: 0.2rem 0; }
.contents > ol > li > a { font-weight: 700; }
.contents > ol > li > a::before { content: counter(toc, decimal-leading-zero); display: inline-block; min-width: 2rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.toc-findings { list-style: none; margin: 0.2rem 0 0.4rem; padding: 0 0 0 2rem; }
.toc-findings li { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.4; padding: 0.12rem 0; max-width: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4.5rem 1fr; gap: 0 0.5rem; }
.toc-findings .sevname { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); padding-top: 0.12rem; }

/* Cards */
.cards { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 10.5rem), 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; }
.cards li { max-width: none; margin: 0; }
.card { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 14px; padding: 0.9rem 1rem 0.95rem; background: var(--panel); height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; margin: 0; }
.card dt { order: 2; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--muted); }
.card dd { display: contents; }
.card .sub { order: 3; }
.card .n { order: 1; }
.card .n { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 2.1rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; display: block; }
.card .n.words { font-size: 1.35rem; padding-top: 0.45rem; }
.card .sub { display: block; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.35; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
.cardwrap { display: block; }
.panel { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--panel); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
.panel h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
.panel p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.note { border-left: 6px solid var(--amber); background: var(--panel); border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
.note h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
.note p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.notice { border: 1px dashed var(--muted); border-radius: 10px; padding: 0.7rem 1rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.worked { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
.worked li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }

/* Findings */
.group-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 2.25rem 0 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule); }
.group-head h3 { margin: 0; }
.group-head .count { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
article.finding { position: relative; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 8px solid var(--muted); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.15rem 1.4rem 0.7rem 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; background: var(--paper); }
article.finding.f-blocker { border-left-color: var(--blocker); }
article.finding.f-major { border-left-color: var(--major); }
article.finding.f-minor { border-left-color: var(--minor); }
article.finding.f-info { border-left-color: var(--info); }
.f-badges { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; max-width: none; }
article.finding h4 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
.f-where { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
dl.facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(7.5rem, max-content) 1fr; gap: 0.35rem 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }
dl.facts dt { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); padding-top: 0.2rem; }
dl.facts dd { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
dl.facts.small { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
ol.steps { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
ol.steps li { padding-left: 0.3rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
ol.steps li::marker { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; color: var(--muted); }
figure { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px; }
figcaption { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.4rem; }
.outcome { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.f-body { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
details.tech { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 1rem; padding: 0.5rem 0 0.4rem; }
details.tech summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--muted); padding: 0.2rem 0; }
details.tech summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 3px; }
details.tech dl { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

/* Tables */
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.96rem; margin: 0; }
caption { text-align: left; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; padding: 0 0 0.5rem; }
th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
thead th { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
tbody th { font-weight: 700; }
.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
td code { white-space: normal; }
.help { font-weight: 400; }
h3.sub { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem; }

footer { margin-top: 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1.25rem 0 2.5rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--muted); }
footer p { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }

@media (max-width: 40rem) {
  .cover-body.has-mascot { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .mascot { width: 7rem; }
  dl.facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
  dl.facts dd { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  article.finding { padding: 1rem 1rem 0.5rem; }
}

@media print {
  :root { color-scheme: light; }
  @page { size: A4; margin: 20mm 16mm 20mm;
    @top-left { content: "{{.Title}}"; font: 8pt/1 "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next", Arial, sans-serif; color: #55524d; vertical-align: bottom; padding-bottom: 4mm; }
    @top-right { content: "{{if .Client}}Prepared for {{.Client}}{{else}}Audit report{{end}}"; font: 8pt/1 "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next", Arial, sans-serif; color: #55524d; vertical-align: bottom; padding-bottom: 4mm; }
    @bottom-left { content: "Made with dummyrun {{.ToolVersion}}"; font: 8pt/1 "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next", Arial, sans-serif; color: #55524d; vertical-align: top; padding-top: 4mm; }
    @bottom-right { content: "Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages); font: 8pt/1 "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next", Arial, sans-serif; color: #55524d; vertical-align: top; padding-top: 4mm; }
  }
  @page :first { @top-left { content: none; } @top-right { content: none; } }
  body { font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.5; }
  * { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
  .skip { display: none; }
  .wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .cover { padding: 0; border: 0; min-height: 235mm; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; break-after: page; }
  .cover > .wrap { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .cover-top { margin-bottom: 22mm; }
  .cover h1 { font-size: 36pt; }
  .cover-body { margin-top: auto; }
  .contents { padding-top: 0; }
  section { padding-top: 0; break-before: page; }
  section.flow { break-before: auto; padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  h2, h3, h4, h5 { break-after: avoid; }
  article.finding, figure, tr, .card, .panel, .note, .overview { break-inside: avoid; }
  thead { display: table-header-group; }
  .table-wrap { overflow: visible; }
  a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; }
  article.finding { border-radius: 6px; }
  details.tech:not([open])::details-content { content-visibility: visible; display: block; }
  details.tech summary { list-style: none; }
  details.tech summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  figure img { max-height: 100mm; object-fit: contain; object-position: left top; }
  footer { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to the report</a>

<header class="cover">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="cover-top">
{{- /* Agencies: put your own logo inside .cover-brand, or replace the whole element. */}}
<span class="cover-brand">
<img class="logo-light" src="{{asset "lockup-horizontal.svg"}}" alt="Dummy Run" width="351" height="88">
<img class="logo-dark" src="{{asset "lockup-horizontal-dark.svg"}}" alt="Dummy Run" width="351" height="88">
</span>
</div>
<p class="eyebrow">Audit report</p>
<h1>{{.Title}}</h1>
{{if .Client}}<p class="for">Prepared for <strong>{{.Client}}</strong></p>{{end}}
<dl class="cover-meta">
{{- range .Scope.Targets}}{{if .BaseURL}}
<div><dt>Target</dt><dd>{{.BaseURL}}</dd></div>
{{- end}}{{end}}
{{- if .Scope.StartedAt}}
<div><dt>Tested</dt><dd>{{period .Scope}}</dd></div>
{{- end}}
<div><dt>Report date</dt><dd>{{longDate .Date}}</dd></div>
{{- if .Baseline}}
<div><dt>Compared with</dt><dd>{{.Baseline.Title}}, {{longDate .Baseline.Date}}</dd></div>
{{- end}}
<div><dt>Findings included</dt><dd>{{cap .Basis}}</dd></div>
</dl>
<div class="cover-body has-mascot">
<div>
<p class="cover-lead">{{lead .Summary.Text}}</p>
{{- $segs := segments .Summary}}
<div class="overview" role="group" aria-labelledby="ov-title">
<p class="ov-title" id="ov-title">Problems found, by severity</p>
{{- if $segs}}
<svg class="bar" viewBox="0 0 100 10" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="{{range $i, $s := $segs}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$s.Count}} {{$s.Severity}}{{end}}">
{{- range $segs}}<rect class="seg seg-{{.Severity}}" x="{{.X}}" y="0" width="{{.W}}" height="10"/>{{end -}}
</svg>
{{- end}}
<ul class="chips">
{{- range $sev := severities}}{{$n := index $.Summary.BySeverity $sev}}
<li><span class="chip b-{{$sev}}{{if not $n}} is-zero{{end}}"><b>{{$n}}</b> {{cap $sev}}</span></li>
{{- end}}
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<img class="mascot" src="{{asset "dummy-reading.svg"}}" alt="" width="152" height="182">
</div>
</div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">
<nav class="contents" aria-labelledby="h-contents">
<h2 id="h-contents">Contents</h2>
<ol>
<li><a href="#summary">Summary</a></li>
<li><a href="#findings">Findings</a>
{{- if .Findings}}
<ul class="toc-findings">
{{- range sevGroups .Findings}}{{$g := .}}
{{- range .Items}}
<li><span class="sevname">{{cap $g.Severity}}</span><a href="#f-{{.Index}}">{{.Finding.Title}}</a></li>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
</ul>
{{- end}}
</li>
{{- if .Axe}}
<li><a href="#axe-sweep">Axe sweep and layout checks</a></li>
{{- end}}
{{- if .Baseline}}
<li><a href="#baseline">Since the baseline</a></li>
{{- end}}
<li><a href="#method">How it was tested</a></li>
<li><a href="#limits">What this report is not</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>

<main id="main">

<section id="summary" class="flow" aria-labelledby="h-summary">
<h2 id="h-summary">Summary</h2>
{{if .Summary.NotReviewed}}<p class="notice"><strong>Not reviewed:</strong> {{plural .Summary.NotReviewed "finding" "findings"}}. A model reported what it found and no person has checked the evidence.</p>{{end}}
{{range .Warnings}}<p class="notice">{{.}}</p>{{end}}

<h3 class="sub">The key numbers</h3>
<ul class="cards">
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Problems found</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Summary.FindingsTotal}}</span><span class="sub">{{.Summary.Confirmed}} confirmed by a person</span></dd></dl></li>
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Runs</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Scope.Runs.Total}}</span><span class="sub">{{.Scope.Runs.Completed}} completed</span></dd></dl></li>
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Personas</dt><dd><span class="n">{{len .Scope.Personas}}</span><span class="sub">fictional users</span></dd></dl></li>
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Routes visited</dt><dd><span class="n">{{len .Scope.Routes}}</span>{{if .Coverage.RouteUniverse}}<span class="sub">of {{.Coverage.RouteUniverse}} known</span>{{end}}</dd></dl></li>
{{- if .Axe}}
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Pages in the axe sweep</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Axe.Pages}}</span><span class="sub">{{.Axe.FailingNodes}} failing {{if eq .Axe.FailingNodes 1}}element{{else}}elements{{end}}</span></dd></dl></li>
{{- end}}
{{- if .Baseline}}
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Since the baseline</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Summary.New}}</span><span class="sub">new, {{.Summary.StillPresent}} still present, {{.Summary.Fixed}} not seen again</span></dd></dl></li>
{{- end}}
</ul>

<div class="panel">
<h3>How sure you can be</h3>
<p>{{howSure .Coverage}}</p>
{{- if and .Coverage.Available .Coverage.SampleCoverage}}
<p class="muted">Sample coverage is {{f2 .Coverage.SampleCoverage}}. The method is under <a href="#method">How it was tested</a>.</p>
{{- end}}
</div>

{{if .Scope.Runs.Total}}
<h3 class="sub">What was tested</h3>
<dl class="facts">
{{- range .Scope.Targets}}
<dt>Target</dt><dd>{{.BaseURL}}, build <code>{{.Build}}</code> ({{.BuildKind}}), {{.Environment}}</dd>
{{- end}}
<dt>Personas</dt><dd>{{range $i, $p := .Scope.Personas}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$p.ID}} ({{$p.Role}}){{end}}</dd>
<dt>Scenarios</dt><dd>{{range $i, $s := .Scope.Scenarios}}{{if $i}}; {{end}}{{$s.Title}}{{end}}</dd>
<dt>Browsers</dt><dd>{{range $i, $b := .Scope.Browsers}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$b.Name}} {{$b.Version}}{{end}}</dd>
{{- if .Axe}}
<dt>Axe sweep</dt><dd>{{.Axe.Pages}} {{if eq .Axe.Pages 1}}page{{else}}pages{{end}} in {{.Axe.Runs}} {{if eq .Axe.Runs 1}}setting{{else}}settings{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>
{{else}}
<h3 class="sub">What was tested</h3>
<p>No persona runs were given. This report holds the axe sweep only.</p>
{{end}}

{{if .Worked}}
<h3 class="sub" id="worked">What worked</h3>
<p>Personas also reported what went well. A model wrote these notes and no person has checked them, so they are observations and not findings.</p>
<ul class="worked">
{{- range .Worked}}
<li>{{.Text}} <span class="muted">({{.Runs}} of {{$.Scope.Runs.Total}} runs; {{join .Personas}})</span></li>
{{- end}}
</ul>
{{end}}

<aside class="note" aria-labelledby="h-note">
<h3 id="h-note">Read this as a sample</h3>
<p>This report tells you what the runs met. It is not a certificate and it does not say the site meets a standard. A problem nobody ran into is not in it. <a href="#limits">What this report is not</a> says more.</p>
</aside>
</section>

<section id="findings" aria-labelledby="h-findings">
<h2 id="h-findings">Findings</h2>
<p>The findings are sorted by severity, then by the number of runs that found them. Each is a distinct problem, and one found in several runs appears once.</p>
{{if not .Findings}}<p>This report has no persona findings.</p>{{end}}
{{range sevGroups .Findings}}{{$g := .}}
<div class="group-head"><h3 id="g-{{$g.Severity}}">{{cap $g.Severity}}</h3><span class="count">{{plural (len $g.Items) "finding" "findings"}}</span></div>
{{range .Items}}{{$f := .Finding}}{{$i := .Index}}
<article class="finding f-{{$f.Severity}}" id="f-{{$i}}" aria-labelledby="f-{{$i}}-t">
<p class="f-badges"><span class="badge b-{{$f.Severity}}">{{cap $f.Severity}}</span><span class="badge st-{{$f.Status}}">{{statusText $f.Status}}</span>
{{- if $f.Baseline}}<span class="badge bl-{{$f.Baseline}}">{{baselineText $f.Baseline}}</span>{{end}}</p>
<h4 id="f-{{$i}}-t">{{$f.Title}}</h4>
{{- $place := placeText $f.Route $f.Locus}}
{{if $place}}<p class="f-where">{{upper $place}}{{if $f.Route}} <code>{{$f.Route}}</code>{{end}}</p>{{end}}
{{- if $f.Body}}
<p class="f-body">{{$f.Body}}</p>
{{- end}}
<dl class="facts">
{{- with whereText $f}}
<dt>Where it is</dt><dd>{{.}}</dd>
{{- end}}
{{- if $f.Quote}}
<dt>On the page</dt><dd><q>{{$f.Quote}}</q></dd>
{{- end}}
{{- if $f.Symptom}}
<dt>What went wrong</dt><dd>{{symptomText $f.Symptom}}</dd>
{{- end}}
<dt>Who hit it</dt><dd>{{whoText $ $f}}</dd>
{{- if $f.State}}
<dt>When</dt><dd>{{$f.State}}</dd>
{{- end}}
{{- if $f.WCAG}}
<dt>WCAG 2.2</dt><dd>{{wcagText $f.WCAG}}</dd>
{{- end}}
{{- if $f.Fix}}
<dt>How to fix it</dt><dd>{{$f.Fix}}</dd>
{{- end}}
<dt>Review</dt><dd>{{if eq $f.Status "confirmed"}}Confirmed{{if $f.Reviewers}} by {{join $f.Reviewers}}{{end}}{{if $f.ReviewedAt}} on {{longDate $f.ReviewedAt}}{{end}}{{if $f.Reason}}. Reason: {{$f.Reason}}{{end}}{{else}}Not reviewed. No person has checked this finding.{{end}}</dd>
{{- if $f.HelpURL}}
<dt>Fix guidance</dt><dd><a href="{{$f.HelpURL}}">{{$f.HelpURL}}</a></dd>
{{- end}}
</dl>
<h5>How to reproduce</h5>
<ol class="steps">
{{- range reproSteps $f}}
<li>{{.}}</li>
{{- end}}
</ol>
<p class="outcome"><strong>What goes wrong:</strong> {{$f.Title}}</p>
{{range $f.Screenshots}}{{$u := shot .}}
{{if $u}}<figure><img src="{{$u}}" alt="Screenshot: {{shotCaption $f .}}"><figcaption>{{shotCaption $f .}}.{{with lookAt $f}} <strong>{{.}}</strong>{{end}}</figcaption></figure>{{else}}<p class="muted">The screenshot for this finding was not found when this report was made.</p>{{end}}
{{end}}
<details class="tech">
<summary>Technical details</summary>
<dl class="facts small">
<dt>Run</dt><dd><code>{{$f.Reproduction.Run}}</code>{{if $f.Reproduction.Steps}}, step{{if gt (len $f.Reproduction.Steps) 1}}s{{end}} {{range $j, $st := $f.Reproduction.Steps}}{{if $j}}, {{end}}{{$st.N}}{{end}}{{end}}</dd>
<dt>Persona</dt><dd><code>{{$f.Reproduction.Persona}}</code>, {{$f.Reproduction.Device}}, {{$f.Reproduction.Browser}}</dd>
<dt>Kind</dt><dd>{{$f.Kind}}</dd>
{{- if $f.Symptom}}
<dt>Symptom</dt><dd><code>{{$f.Symptom}}</code></dd>
{{- end}}
{{- if or $f.Route $f.Locus}}
<dt>Location</dt><dd>{{if $f.Route}}<code>{{$f.Route}}</code>{{end}}{{if $f.Locus}} <code>{{$f.Locus}}</code>{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
<dt>Evidence</dt><dd>{{$f.Evidence}}</dd>
<dt>Fingerprint</dt><dd><code>{{if $f.Fingerprint}}{{$f.Fingerprint}}{{else}}none{{end}}</code></dd>
{{- if gt (len $f.Instances) 1}}
<dt>Also seen in</dt><dd>{{range $j, $in := $f.Instances}}{{if $j}}, {{end}}{{$in.Run}}{{if ne $in.Status "confirmed"}} (not reviewed){{end}}{{end}}</dd>
{{- end}}
{{range $f.Screenshots}}<dt>Screenshot</dt><dd>run {{.Run}}, step {{.Step}}, <code>{{.Path}}</code></dd>
{{end}}
</dl>
</details>
</article>
{{end}}
{{end}}
</section>
{{if .Axe}}
<section id="axe-sweep" aria-labelledby="h-axe">
<h2 id="h-axe">Axe sweep and layout checks</h2>
<p>The sweep ran axe-core {{.Axe.AxeVersion}} with {{.Axe.Tool}} on {{.Axe.Pages}} {{if eq .Axe.Pages 1}}page{{else}}pages{{end}} in {{.Axe.Runs}} {{if eq .Axe.Runs 1}}setting{{else}}settings{{end}} (browser, viewport and colour scheme), on {{join .Axe.Browsers}}. It checked the rules with these tags: {{range .Axe.Tags}}<code>{{.}}</code> {{end}}{{if .Axe.AdviceTags}}. It also checked {{range .Axe.AdviceTags}}<code>{{.}}</code> {{end}}, and lists the rules from those that are not WCAG A or AA rules as advice{{end}}. It found {{.Axe.FailingNodes}} failing {{if eq .Axe.FailingNodes 1}}element{{else}}elements{{end}}{{if .Axe.AllowedNodes}} and set aside {{.Axe.AllowedNodes}} on the allow-list{{end}}.</p>
{{if .Axe.Rules}}
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Rules that failed">
<table>
<caption>Rules that failed</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">Impact</th><th scope="col">WCAG 2.2</th><th scope="col" class="num">Elements</th><th scope="col">Fix guidance</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Axe.Rules}}
<tr>
<th scope="row"><code>{{.Rule}}</code><br><span class="muted help">{{.Help}}</span>{{if .Baseline}}<br><span class="badge bl-{{.Baseline}}">{{baselineText .Baseline}}</span>{{end}}</th>
<td><span class="badge b-{{impactSev .Impact}}">{{if .Impact}}{{cap .Impact}}{{else}}No impact given{{end}}</span></td>
<td>{{if .WCAG}}{{join .WCAG}}{{else}}Not recorded{{end}}</td>
<td class="num">{{.Elements}}</td>
<td>{{if .HelpURL}}<a href="{{.HelpURL}}">How to fix {{.Rule}}</a>{{else}}None recorded{{end}}</td>
</tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Where each rule failed">
<table>
<caption>Where each rule failed</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">Page</th><th scope="col">Elements</th><th scope="col">Settings</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range $r := .Axe.Rules}}{{range $r.Pages}}
<tr><th scope="row"><code>{{$r.Rule}}</code></th><td>{{.URL}}</td><td>{{range $k, $t := .Targets}}{{if $k}}<br>{{end}}<code>{{$t}}</code>{{end}}</td><td>{{range $k, $t := .Settings}}{{if $k}}<br>{{end}}{{$t}}{{end}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{else}}<p>No element failed a rule in the settings tested. That is a statement about the sweep and not about the app.</p>{{end}}
{{if .Axe.NeedsReview}}
<h3 class="sub">Needs a person to check</h3>
<p>Axe cannot decide these rules alone. A person has to look.</p>
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Rules that need review">
<table>
<caption>Rules that need review</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">What it checks</th><th scope="col">WCAG 2.2</th><th scope="col">Pages</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Axe.NeedsReview}}
<tr><th scope="row"><code>{{.Rule}}</code></th><td>{{.Help}}</td><td>{{if .WCAG}}{{join .WCAG}}{{else}}Not recorded{{end}}</td><td>{{range $k, $p := .Pages}}{{if $k}}<br>{{end}}{{$p.URL}}{{end}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{end}}
{{if .Axe.Advice}}
<h3 class="sub">Advice beyond WCAG A and AA</h3>
<p>These are axe's best-practice rules that are not WCAG A or AA rules (a few are WCAG AAA). They are not WCAG A or AA failures and are not counted above, but each one makes the site harder to use for someone.</p>
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Best-practice advice">
<table>
<caption>Best-practice advice</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">What it checks</th><th scope="col" class="num">Elements</th><th scope="col">Pages</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Axe.Advice}}
<tr><th scope="row"><code>{{.Rule}}</code></th><td>{{.Help}}{{if .HelpURL}} (<a href="{{.HelpURL}}">how to fix</a>){{end}}</td><td class="num">{{.Elements}}</td><td>{{range $k, $p := .Pages}}{{if $k}}<br>{{end}}{{$p.URL}}{{end}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{end}}
{{if .Axe.Errors}}
<h3 class="sub">Pages that could not be tested</h3>
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Page errors">
<table>
<caption>Page errors</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Page</th><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Error</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Axe.Errors}}
<tr><td>{{.URL}}</td><td>{{.Setting}}</td><td>{{.Message}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{end}}
</section>
{{end}}
{{if .Baseline}}
<section id="baseline" aria-labelledby="h-baseline">
<h2 id="h-baseline">Since the baseline</h2>
<p>The baseline is the report titled {{.Baseline.Title}} of {{longDate .Baseline.Date}}. Findings are matched by fingerprint. A finding the baseline had and this report did not find again is marked fixed. A sample can miss a problem that is still there.</p>
<ul class="cards">
<li><dl class="card"><dt>New since the baseline</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Summary.New}}</span></dd></dl></li>
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Still present</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Summary.StillPresent}}</span></dd></dl></li>
<li><dl class="card"><dt>Not seen again</dt><dd><span class="n">{{.Summary.Fixed}}</span></dd></dl></li>
</ul>
{{if .Fixed}}
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Fixed since the baseline">
<table>
<caption>Fixed since the baseline</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Severity</th><th scope="col">Problem</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Fixed}}
<tr><td>{{cap .Severity}}</td><th scope="row">{{.Title}}</th><td>{{if eq .Source "axe"}}Axe sweep{{else}}Persona run{{end}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{else}}<p>Nothing from the baseline is missing from this report.</p>{{end}}
</section>
{{end}}
<section id="method" aria-labelledby="h-method">
<h2 id="h-method">How it was tested</h2>
<p>Each run signs one fictional user, called a persona, in to the app in a real browser. The persona works through a scenario and reports what broke, what confused it and what its role should not have seen. Findings are folded together when they share a fingerprint, which is a hash of the route, the control and the kind of symptom.</p>
{{if .Scope.Runs.Total}}
<dl class="facts">
<dt>Period</dt><dd>{{.Scope.StartedAt}} to {{.Scope.EndedAt}}</dd>
<dt>Runs</dt><dd>{{.Scope.Runs.Total}} in total: {{.Scope.Runs.Completed}} completed, {{.Scope.Runs.Blocked}} blocked, {{.Scope.Runs.Errored}} errored and {{.Scope.Runs.BudgetExhausted}} out of budget</dd>
<dt>Model cost</dt><dd>{{usd .Scope.Cost.USD}} over {{.Scope.Cost.ModelCalls}} model calls ({{.Scope.Cost.InputTokens}} input and {{.Scope.Cost.OutputTokens}} output tokens){{if .Scope.Cost.UnpricedRuns}}. {{.Scope.Cost.UnpricedRuns}} runs used a model with no price, so the cost is a floor{{end}}</dd>
<dt>Routes visited</dt><dd>{{len .Scope.Routes}}{{if .Scope.Routes}}: {{range .Scope.Routes}}<code>{{.}}</code> {{end}}{{end}}</dd>
</dl>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Target and build">
<table>
<caption>Target and build</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Environment</th><th scope="col">Build</th><th scope="col">Adapter</th><th scope="col" class="num">Runs</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Scope.Targets}}
<tr><td>{{.BaseURL}}</td><td>{{.Environment}}</td><td><code>{{.Build}}</code> ({{.BuildKind}})</td><td>{{.Adapter}}</td><td class="num">{{.Runs}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Personas and the dimensions they varied">
<table>
<caption>Personas and the dimensions they varied</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Persona</th><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Device</th><th scope="col">Dimensions</th><th scope="col" class="num">Runs</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Scope.Personas}}
<tr><th scope="row">{{.ID}}</th><td>{{.Role}}</td><td>{{join .Devices}}</td><td>{{if .Dimensions}}{{join .Dimensions}}{{else}}None recorded{{end}}</td><td class="num">{{.Runs}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scenarios and whether the persona did what it came to do">
<table>
<caption>Scenarios and whether the persona did what it came to do</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Scenario</th><th scope="col" class="num">Runs</th><th scope="col" class="num">Yes</th><th scope="col" class="num">Partly</th><th scope="col" class="num">No</th><th scope="col" class="num">Not recorded</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Scope.Scenarios}}
<tr><th scope="row">{{.Title}}</th><td class="num">{{.Runs}}</td><td class="num">{{.GoalMet}}</td><td class="num">{{.GoalPartly}}</td><td class="num">{{.GoalNotMet}}</td><td class="num">{{.GoalUnknown}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Browsers">
<table>
<caption>Browsers</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Browser</th><th scope="col">Version</th><th scope="col" class="num">Runs</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Scope.Browsers}}
<tr><td>{{.Name}}</td><td>{{.Version}}</td><td class="num">{{.Runs}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Models and providers">
<table>
<caption>Models and providers</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col" class="num">Runs</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .Scope.Models}}
<tr><td>{{.Model}}</td><td>{{.Kind}}</td><td>{{.Region}}</td><td class="num">{{.Runs}}</td></tr>
{{- end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{else}}
<p>No persona runs were given. This report holds the axe sweep only.</p>
{{end}}

<h3 class="sub" id="coverage">Coverage</h3>
{{if .Coverage.Available}}
<p>These numbers come from <code>dummyrun coverage</code> over the same runs. They say how much the sample can tell you.</p>
<dl class="facts">
<dt>Counted</dt><dd>{{.Coverage.Basis}}</dd>
<dt>Completed runs</dt><dd>{{.Coverage.CompletedRuns}}</dd>
<dt>Distinct problems seen</dt><dd>{{.Coverage.Observed}}</dd>
<dt>Still unfound</dt><dd>{{if .Coverage.UnfoundAtLeast}}At least {{f1 .Coverage.UnfoundAtLeast}} (Chao2 lower bound of {{f1 .Coverage.TotalAtLeast}} in total, {{.Coverage.Form}} form){{else}}Not estimable from these runs{{end}}</dd>
<dt>Sample coverage</dt><dd>{{if .Coverage.SampleCoverage}}{{f2 .Coverage.SampleCoverage}}{{else}}Not estimable{{end}}</dd>
<dt>New per extra run</dt><dd>{{if .Coverage.NewPerExtraRun}}{{f2 .Coverage.NewPerExtraRun}}{{else}}Not estimable{{end}}</dd>
{{- if .Coverage.RouteUniverse}}
<dt>Routes visited</dt><dd>{{.Coverage.RoutesVisited}} of {{.Coverage.RouteUniverse}} known routes</dd>
{{- end}}
<dt>Stopping rule</dt><dd>{{.Coverage.StoppingRule}}</dd>
</dl>
<h4>How to read these numbers</h4>
<ul>
<li>The Chao2 figure is a floor. The real number of problems is at least that high. It is never a count of what remains.</li>
<li>Sample coverage is the share of the chance of finding a problem that sits in problems already found. Below 0.50 do not extrapolate from it.</li>
<li>New problems per extra run is how many new problems one more run is expected to find. A low figure suggests more runs will add little.</li>
<li>With fewer than 5 completed runs the estimates are weak. The stopping rule needs 4 completed runs in each group.</li>
</ul>
{{if .Coverage.Warnings}}<h4>Cautions</h4>
<ul>
{{- range .Coverage.Warnings}}
<li>{{.}}</li>
{{- end}}
</ul>{{end}}
{{else}}
<p class="notice">Coverage was not computed. {{.Coverage.Unavailable}}</p>
{{end}}
</section>

<section id="limits" aria-labelledby="h-limits">
<h2 id="h-limits">What this report is not</h2>
<ul>
{{- range .Limits}}
<li>{{.}}</li>
{{- end}}
</ul>
</section>
</main>
<footer>
<p>Made with dummyrun {{.ToolVersion}} on {{longDate .Date}}. This report is one file and loads nothing from the network.</p>
<p>Set in Space Grotesk and Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.</p>
</footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
